{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the angel of Elohim went.</b> To separate between the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel, and to catch the arrows and ballistae of the Egyptians. Everywhere it says 'the angel of YHWH,' but here 'the angel of Elohim' — Elohim everywhere means only 'judge'; this teaches that Israel were on trial at that hour, whether to be saved or to perish with the Egyptians (ibid.)." "<b>And the pillar of cloud moved.</b> When it grew dark and the pillar of cloud merged with the pillar of fire, the cloud did not depart as it was accustomed to depart entirely in the evening, but rather moved and went behind them to bring darkness upon the Egyptians."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:09.689053924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}